DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270302
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270303
SUMMARY:SAMPLE-DRP-004: Offices whose building wants our certificate (coi_
 required y (you)
DESCRIPTION:Offices whose building wants our certificate (coi_required yes
  or unsure): request it from our carrier at least 10 business days before 
 that office's first drop (legal pack file 12)\, only once general liabilit
 y is bound.\nLog it in: offices: building_coi_status\, building_coi_date
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:SAMPLE-DRP-004-paid@campaign-ops
DTSTAMP:20261024T120000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270309
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270310
SUMMARY:SAMPLE-DRP-004: Payment lands in the business account (brand)
DESCRIPTION:Payment lands in the business account: log paid_date and paid_
 amount on invoices. Founding: due within five business days of the invoice
  and before shipping\; standard: the first 50% on signing. Five business d
 ays late: you decide whether to cancel and refund (file 10\, section 3).\n
 Log it in: invoices: paid_date\, paid_amount_usd\, method\, bank_reference
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:SAMPLE-DRP-004-coi_check@campaign-ops
DTSTAMP:20261024T120000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270309
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270310
SUMMARY:SAMPLE-DRP-004: Brand's certificate in (you)
DESCRIPTION:Brand's certificate in: the five-minute check in legal pack fi
 le 11. Tick coi_check_ok on brands. If the policy ends before 12 months af
 ter the window\, diary the renewal certificate.\nLog it in: campaigns: coi
 _received_date\; brands: coi_check_ok\, coi_policy_end_date
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:SAMPLE-DRP-004-release@campaign-ops
DTSTAMP:20261024T120000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270309
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270310
SUMMARY:SAMPLE-DRP-004: When campaigns shows ship_release RELEASED (pre-sh
 ip payment (you)
DESCRIPTION:When campaigns shows ship_release RELEASED (pre-ship payment i
 n\, agreement signed\, certificate checked\, every office on the route has
  answered)\, send the ship-date email (template 02) the same day and log w
 hat it said. Never confirm a ship date on HOLD. An office that said no and
  cannot be replaced shows as a credit to make ($120 founding\, $150 standa
 rd)\, not a hold. If an office joins or leaves the route before the produc
 t arrives\, the campaign's checks say the units changed: send the revised 
 email the tool drafts\, and log it.\nLog it in: campaigns: ship_release\; 
 ship_email_sent_date\, ship_email_units
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:SAMPLE-DRP-004-direct_plan@campaign-ops
DTSTAMP:20261024T120000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270309
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270310
SUMMARY:SAMPLE-DRP-004: Direct-ship (you and brand)
DESCRIPTION:Direct-ship: send the brand each office's address and case lab
 els (labels.pdf)\, ask for a service that delivers on T\, one tracking num
 ber per office by T-2 (template 02 says it)\, and the reserve shipped to y
 ou by T-5. An office whose front desk will not hold food (receiving not wa
 lk-up\, front_desk_fallback_ok not Y\; the stops tab says so): its cartons
  ship to you with the reserve and you deliver them on T (template 02 lists
  them that way).\nLog it in: stops: carrier_tracking later
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:SAMPLE-DRP-004-ship@campaign-ops
DTSTAMP:20261024T120000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270309
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270310
SUMMARY:SAMPLE-DRP-004: Hard ship-by and cancel-by date (T-10). Approvals 
 due. If T- (brand)
DESCRIPTION:Hard ship-by and cancel-by date (T-10). Approvals due. If T-10
  to T-5 crosses 18 to 31 December\, brands were asked to ship earlier (shi
 p_by_requested).\nLog it in: approvals: reply\, reply_date
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:SAMPLE-DRP-004-receive_ds@campaign-ops
